53 1079 #uuid "be04018e-9849-5afe-9540-e80db3c5e1e0" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424234 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424237 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424244 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424246 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424249 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1077 "selection" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424249 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424254 1079 #uuid "e5967368-9c1c-5296-b137-b9913b855878" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424255 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424251 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424255 1069 "q-110816" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424255 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424255 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $a$ | $2a$ | $\\frac{3a}{2}$ | $3a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424255 1072 #uuid "0c6d1e5f-c8c7-58eb-9372-45bad8d48254" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424255 1074 "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}=\\{2\\},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}=\\{0,1,2,3\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{(2,0),(2,1),(2,2),(2,3)\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2)+f(2,3) & =1 \\\\ a+2a+\\frac{3a}{2}+3a & =1 \\\\ \\frac{15a}{2} & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424256 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424254 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424256 1069 "q-111038" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424256 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424256 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424256 1072 #uuid "663c80f0-fe5e-502f-84c3-e0164d0d760f" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424256 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & \\,+P((X,Y)=(2,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(2,0)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.05+0.15+0.05 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424257 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424252 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424257 1069 "q-111035" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424257 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424257 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(0<Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424257 1072 #uuid "77b7b7f9-a7fd-5ac7-a5d0-130bc06dad6a" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424257 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<Y<2) & =P(Y=1) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(0,1),(1,1)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,1))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424258 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424253 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424258 1069 "q-110814" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424258 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424258 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{a}{3}$ | $a$ | $3a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $4a$ | $\\frac{2a}{3}$ | $\\frac{a}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $a$ | $\\frac{3a}{2}$ | $5a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424258 1072 #uuid "f92de356-71ac-5b5e-9291-a3c3ef80d00b" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true] [17592186424258 1074 "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}=\\{0,1,2\\},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}=\\{0,1,2\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{(0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,0),(1,1),(1,2),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(0,2)+f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}+a+3a+4a+\\frac{2a}{3}+\\frac{a}{2}+a+\\frac{3a}{2}+5a & =1 \\\\ 17a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-04fbecf1-c27f-59ee-850b-c3f175aae366" 17592186424231 "answer-0ecbcc89-8b20-5446-8735-5273eb0286fc" 17592186424232 "answer-1529ce67-67d0-5c1f-a17d-5ea1c1983d56" 17592186424233 "answer-170857b0-1781-50ab-a9f3-dac4f2f65bb0" 17592186424234 "answer-28842ea5-4a23-5bc7-aed2-d9be8492202a" 17592186424235 "answer-301025df-a886-5236-ad98-3b902e2ea82f" 17592186424236 "answer-35532208-e23a-5095-9966-0c7fc84450af" 17592186424237 "answer-3d56e76f-6d74-5301-a933-a1c053d1c57f" 175